 ## Known gaps on macOS
 
-- Hot reload (`ArchiveXL.Reload()`) is disabled. It logs `ArchiveXL.Reload() is not supported on macOS.`
-  Restart the game to pick up changed `.xl` files.
 - At unload, static game handles are leaked on purpose (`LeakAtExit` in
   `src/App/Extensions/ExtensionBase.hpp`), because releasing them after the game has shut down crashed on exit.
 - The macOS game itself does not load mod archives: it never reads `archive/pc/mod/`. ArchiveXL loads that folder
   instead (in name order, like the game does on Windows), so on macOS `.archive` mods need ArchiveXL even when they
   have no `.xl` file.
-- Also off on macOS: the Transmog factory template override, native registration of the two PuppetState enums, and the
-  WorldWidgetComponent limit patch, collision shape deletions in world streaming sectors (whole-actor deletions work),
-  and the nails color fallback read from the character customization state (the color still comes from the nails
-  component). Their addresses or layouts are not verified on macOS.
+- Hot reload, the Transmog factory template override, the PuppetState enums, the WorldWidgetComponent limit patch,
+  collision shape deletions in world streaming sectors and the nails color fallback work as on Windows. They need the
+  RED4ext.SDK address database with the `ResourceLoader_OnUpdate` and `InkWorldLayer_UpdateComponents` entries
+  verified, and an SDK at or after f682fb88 (macOS `CEnum::FromString`). On macOS the WorldWidgetComponent patch
+  rewrites one instruction of the game's code in memory at startup (the file on disk is not changed).
+- Hot reload safety: `ArchiveXL.Reload()` rebuilds the extension state on the main thread while game worker threads
+  run ArchiveXL hooks that read it. One reader/writer lock (`src/App/Extensions/ExtensionGuard.hpp`) keeps them apart:
+  the startup configure/load and the reload hold it exclusively, and the hooks that read reloadable state hold it
+  shared, without waiting for other threads while they hold it. The header lists the guarded hooks and why the others
+  need no guard. While a reload runs, resource loads that reach these hooks wait until it ends (a short stall). Some
+  hooks still race with each other the same way as on Windows (for example customization app overrides and journal
+  mappin resolution); that is unchanged.
 
 ## Troubleshooting
 
